00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.330
Homecoming

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.330
Homecoming

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.330
Homecoming

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.420
Hey, Verde!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.330
What the-

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.340
I'm disappearing.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:01.720
This song will stop me from keeping my true form.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.470
I...

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.480
I wanted to make Aria's dream come true...

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.980
Gaul-sama!

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.980
Shinku!

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.900
Guys!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.480
Hey!

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.480
Hero-sama!

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.410
The song of healing is cleansing him.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.990
Can we stop it?

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.700
He's a demon!

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.500
And an apostle, no less!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.790
I know, but...

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.710
Please, Char.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.880
There are questions that we need to ask him.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.690
Then use your hero stones.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.480
Their defensive fields should block out the power of the song.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.480
All right.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.320
Thanks.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.190
Don't go blaming me later.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.410
Hero stone...

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.030
activate!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.760
I didn't know we could use them like this.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.260
Yeah, I can't hear the song at all.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.770
<i>Gaul, and all his friends...</i>

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.150
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.610
<i>It's all my fault.</i>

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.110
<i>I should've paid more attention to Verde.</i>

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.370
<i>I should've noticed how he felt about me.</i>

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:55.880
<i>All he ever wanted to do was grant my wish of visiting down below.</i>

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.470
Hey, Verde.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.820
I dunno where you came from,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.660
or how all this happened.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:33.410
But let me tell you that no man should ever make a girl cry.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.830
I won't deny that you are to blame for some of this,

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.250
but just saying it isn't going to solve anything.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:46.300
And having a dream is never something to be ashamed of.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.310
<i>I'm sorry, Verde.</i>

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.060
<i>I was so cold towards you.</i>

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.820
It's not your fault, Aria.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.900
I'm a demon...

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.950
An apostle.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.570
<i>That doesn't matter to me.</i>

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.330
<i>You're </i>Verde.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.540
<i>You were always there when I needed someone.</i>

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.130
<i>You were always thinking about me</i>

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.880
<i>and you always tried to help me.</i>

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.050
<i>You'll always be the Verde that I love.</i>

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.480
What?!

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:45.610
Crap!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.990
Hold on!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.610
That light...

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.500
A cursed sword!

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.250
It shattered.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.750
I see.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.000
He was possessed by one, too.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.170
I'm sorry, Aria...

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:11.760
I'm sorry, heroes from down below...

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.280
What's happening?

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.780
Don't worry.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.650
This is a good transformation.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:47.920
Verde will return to his natural form inside this crystal.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:53.970
He may have originally been a high spirit or deity.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.930
The cursed sword turned him into an apostle of disease.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:05.610
It would normally take many, many years for him to completely recover.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:11.280
But if you stayed with him and sang to him every day...

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.070
It might not take that long.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.450
That's right.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:17.990
Okay!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.910
Your voice!

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.460
It's so beautiful.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.110
Aria-san!

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.950
I'm sorry for troubling you, Rebecca-san.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.870
And you too, princess from down below.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.950
My name is Millhiore.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.620
I'm pleased to meet you, diva of the Skysea.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.290
As the diva of the star festival, I must sing the song of healing.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.010
Princess Millhiore, would you care to join me?

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:12.840
Yes!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.970
I would be delighted to!

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.540
Thank you for the ride, Couvre-sama.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.540
Anytime, Prince!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:04.060
People from down below, and Char, the dragon priestess...

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.310
Thank you very much for your help.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:12.820
After a long search, I found the flame dragon safe and sound.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.820
Whee!

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.660
Now we've got nothing to worry about.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.830
It's time for us to part ways.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.120
Yes.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.700
But first...

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.950
Right away!

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:30.920
I present to you my token of gratitude for your heroism.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:45.600
What is he?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.980
Your people call his kind "mythical beasts."

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.440
They're the thing of legends!

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.320
They say they're messengers of the gods

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.740
and just looking at them brings great fortune!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:01.870
He and Pega are the only 
mythical beasts I've seen in my entire life.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.490
Pega is a mythical beast, too?!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.910
Yeah, they looked just like each other before!

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.380
He becomes just as cool when he transforms!

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:16.510
As a symbol of our friendship, I will bestow him upon you.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.760
Oh, to me?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.140
It looks like he likes you, Prince Gaul.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.730
Brilliant!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.190
You look great together, Lord Gaul!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:36.530
Then we at Galette shall take good care of him in the name of the Tripartite Alliance.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.030
Yes, that would be splendid.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:44.780
A mythical beast seems like one hell of a responsibility.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Huh?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:11.390
Bye everyone!

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:13.440
See you!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.440
Farewell!

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:19.990
Lord Gaul!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.450
Aria-san's over there.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.410
Yeah.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.460
Couvre, could you get us closer to her?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.710
Sure!

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.670
We'd all better give her a proper goodbye.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.710
No, Lord Gaul.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.210
Huh?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.260
She saved your life.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.630
Go by <i>yourself.</i>

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.720
Off you go!

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.720
Off you go!

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.020
You guys...

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:07.950
Looks like I owe you another one.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:14.040
You saved Verde and me.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.670
There's a lot that I want to tell you...

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.470
How should I thank you?

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.550
No need for that.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:32.180
We helped each other and did some exploring together.

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.940
It's not just me and you. We're <i>all</i> friends now.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.570
Verde included, of course.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.320
Will I ever see you again?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.320
I'd like it if that happened.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.910
So I promise I'll come back.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.120
Can I visit you, too?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.950
Of course!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:52.830
Right...

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.460
guys?!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:01.090
If you want to see someone,
 that's already enough of a reason!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:07.340
There's no need to come up with excuses when you really, really miss someone!

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:10.850
Thanks, everyone!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.730
I love you all!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.410
You two seemed to be getting along quite well, Gaul.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.870
Not really.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.870
Just said bye, that's all.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.000
Yeah, sure.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.000
They were so cute together!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.000
I know!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.800
I hope Aria-san can come visit us sometime.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.460
Indeed.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.130
No distance can break a truly strong friendship.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:55.140
But then again, you've got to see each other 
once in a while to keep that friendship strong.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.640
That's right!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.480
We're almost outside.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.980
The Flame Dragon should be just outside.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:06.400
All right!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.170
Flame Dragon!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.420
Thank you for everything!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.410
It's time to say goodbye.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.160
You're welcome to visit again anytime!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.080
The Skysea will always...

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.950
welcome you!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.750
It was a long journey,

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.340
but everyone's safe and sound, 
and the world is at peace again!

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:10.630
I wish I'd gotten some more action, though.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:13.300
Don't you agree, Eclair?

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:15.140
W-Well...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.850
Less action <i>does</i> mean less harm done.

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:24.860
We've done well to bring peace back without making sacrifices.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.610
Definitely!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.360
Now, time to break through the clouds!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.450
Wow!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.870
I didn't know that these lights came below the clouds!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.080
It's so pretty.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.870
I've never seen this before.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:47.960
I've only ever heard of stories myself.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.260
Our people down below must be seeing this, too.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:54.640
I bet they're baffled about what's happening.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:08.400
<i>This marked the end of our adventure in the Skysea.</i>

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:16.160
<i>Our lords held an international broadcast explaining the lights that would fall from the sky for several days...</i>

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:23.370
These lights are gifts from the Starwhale, who lives in the Skysea.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.790
It is completely harmless, so don't worry about it!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:30.500
This is a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:34.590
Once night falls, the lights will be splendid for some cold ale!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.810
This trip went by so quickly again.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.940
It was very fun and eventful, though!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.150
Will you come back again soon?

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.110
Yeah!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.910
We'll come back for short breaks,

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.950
and we'll be back on weekends for war shows too.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:05.080
I did a lot of vacationing this time around,

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:09.040
so I'd better put on some good shows like a real hero next time I come back!

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.710
As a lord, I'll do the same!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:16.340
And I'll hurry up and properly make myself a lord!

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:17.510
Good luck!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.970
I'll help out where I can!

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:19.890
Thanks!

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:23.600
I don't feel terribly sad to leave this time.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.640
Same here.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:30.360
It's because we can talk and meet each other anytime now.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:34.940
It's when you go home alone that it really hits you!

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:39.410
I'd make a call right away!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.620
Yeah, me too!

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:45.660
Those two sure get along, huh?

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.710
You're right.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.000
Well, then...

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.000
Why don't we get along

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.710
as two apprentices of the hero king?

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:55.630
Sure!

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:01.010
Did I forget anything?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.770
Here you go, Nanami-chan.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.730
It's from Lief.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.390
Thanks!

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:13.980
You can just come pick up whatever you forget anyway.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:18.280
If it's something Cheney can carry, he'll bring it to you.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.490
You're right,

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.410
but I want to tidy up a bit before I leave.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:29.410
A hero needs some dignity, after all.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.170
A-Absolutely!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.880
Now, let's get this room cleaned up!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.420
All right!

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:41.180
I'll see you again, Hero Rebecca!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.840
Okay, Cou-sama!

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.930
I'll be back soon!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.690
Have you forgotten anything?

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.940
Nope!

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.690
It was quite the hassle when you arrived this time.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.940
Hopefully the return trip won't be as bad.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.320
Don't worry!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.700
I'll be back here real soon anyway!

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.200
Good.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.700
Say, Shinku.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:09.700
Yes?

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:13.580
Do you remember what Rebecca-san 
and Nanami-san were telling Aria-san?

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.210
"There's no need to come up with
excuses when you miss someone!"

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.170
Yeah?

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:24.930
Do you remember saying that to Rebecca-san before?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.640
Huh?

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:30.100
Um... that must've been a long time ago.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.850
Maybe I said it... but maybe I didn't?

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:39.230
Rebecca-san would always miss you, and she was happy to see you during each and every break.

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:43.610
But she'd be worried that you wanted to be with your other friends,

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:50.870
or that you were bored being with her because she wasn't the sporty type,

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.420
and she wasn't completely comfortable.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:57.670
Yeah, she used to be really quiet back then.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:01.760
But then, you told her:

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:05.430
"If you miss me, just come and see me."

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:10.020
"Just being with you makes me really happy."

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:18.770
She said she's never forgotten those words once.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.780
I'm starting to remember.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:28.700
I haven't spent a very long time with you, but...

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.160
I really do miss you,

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.540
and I want to be by your side.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.670
I do, too.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.550
So I'll be back as soon as I can.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.510
I promise.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:48.800
Okay!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.650
Did we make it back all right?

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.110
Yeah.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.610
What about Becky?

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:07.910
I'll give her a call.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.160
Hey, Shinku?

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.990
I'm good.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.790
I'm back in one piece!

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.920
That's good to hear!

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.670
Talk to you later.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:21.920
Well, we'd better take care of our earthly duties

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.760
and go back to Flonyard again!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.720
Yeah!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.050
There's lots of schoolwork and sports to be done!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.930
Better get started on that love life, too!

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.930
That's none of your business!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.310
<i>This concludes our autumn adventure.</i>

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:40.560
<i>But we have time in the coming winter and spring!</i>

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:45.280
<i>We'll be going back there,</i>

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:50.280
<i>to our second home, where there are people whom we treasure...</i>

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:52.030
<i>To Flonyard!</i>

